Title: She Drew the Demon Lord
Episode: 1 - The Unveiling
Format: 2D anime vertical micro drama, 9:16, about 60 seconds
Draft date: 2026-10-19

INT. PALACE - THRONE HALL - DAY

[[HOOK: Lady Seren rips Mei's painting in half in front of the whole court.]]

Silk rips. LADY SEREN (22, silver crown braid, white and pale-blue gown) tears a painted scroll in half above the green jade floor.

On her knees below the dais, MEI (19, an ink smudge on her cheek, grey apprentice robe, red hair cord) catches one half before it lands.

SEREN
A servant painting the Crown Prince? Burn it.

MEI
(quietly)
Then burn it before midnight.

SEREN
(laughing)
Or what?

Courtiers laugh behind their sleeves. On the throne steps, CROWN PRINCE JUN (24, crimson robe, gold crown pin) watches with his arms folded.

MEI (V.O.)
Everything I paint wakes at midnight. Today I painted in daylight.

[[TWIST: Mei's spilled ink starts moving on its own.]]

Black ink spills from her overturned ink stone and runs uphill across the jade, toward Seren's white hem.

SEREN
Clean that.

MEI
It isn't mine anymore.

The ink rises into a long black hand. Its fingers close around Seren's ankle.

[[PAYOFF: the court that laughed at Mei falls silent and backs away.]]

Seren shrieks. The courtiers scramble back against the red pillars. The guards' swords shake in their hands.

JUN
(rising)
Who painted that?

Seren points a shaking finger at Mei.

SEREN
Her. The servant.

[[CLIFFHANGER - arrival: the demon lord rises from the ink and asks who woke him.]]

The ink pours upward into a tall man: RAKHAN (waist-long black hair dripping like wet paint, gold eyes, black robe edged in red, a cracked jade collar). The light in the hall dims around him, all but his eyes.

RAKHAN
Three hundred years in a painting.

His gold eyes sweep the court.

RAKHAN (CONT'D)
Who woke me?

Every head turns to Mei.

CUT TO BLACK.
